WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.690
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.990
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.700
but also in crime.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.950
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.490
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.540
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.190
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.990
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:58.990
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.370
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.250
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.210
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:18.430
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:25.020
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:31.360
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:37.150
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:43.700
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:49.380
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:01.100
Red Labor Landing

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.150
Unit 2, end of shift.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.260
The Doshka arrives in Sakata
tomorrow night.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:39.970
The committee has
unanimously agreed to the plan.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.050
Go straight to the site.
Don't return to your apartment.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:44.810
Good luck.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.550
Hold it! Hold it!

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.220
Halt!

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.020
Public safety? The fools.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:40.610
Sakata.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.570
- Sakata.
- Sakata? In Yamagata?

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:45.780
Yes, that Sakata.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.160
Sorry, but my
son's birthday is tonight.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.960
Your son will have many birthdays.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.710
But you'll never get back
a life that you lose.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.080
Ain't that right?

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.260
Mind if I take the toll road?

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.850
I'm Takahata, of Public Safety,
International Division, Section 1.

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:14.810
So, what does Public Safety want?

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:17.110
There was an incident
last night.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:20.480
A suspicious man
that we'd been tailing...

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:25.200
attacked one of our agents
who was pursuing him at the time...

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:28.700
stole his gun, and fled in a taxi.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:30.870
This is the man.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.750
Ichoku Inubashiri.
Born in Kamata, Ota Ward, Tokyo.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:35.830
He's 28 years old.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.670
In 1993, he joined
the Ground Defense Force.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:39.920
Eight years later...

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:42.970
he transferred to the
newly created Flight Labor team.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:44.680
During this time...

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.760
he became a sympathizer of the
"Home of the Sea" terrorist group.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.890
After his discharge, he joined with
this anti-government organization.

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:52.520
Arrested eight times,

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.810
but released each time
due to insufficient evidence.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:59.270
In Utsunomiya, his taxi
ran out of gas and he dumped it.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.030
He then hijacked
a passing motorcycle.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:05.320
He smashed through a patrol unit
that tried to stop him...

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:09.450
and he continued to Shirakawa,
Fukushima, Yonezawa, Sagae...

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:11.950
ignoring traffic lights
and driving recklessly.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:15.210
He ate in Tsuruoka,
but skipped out on the bill.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:18.630
This morning, he slipped
into Sakata and disappeared.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:20.590
How flamboyant.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.760
Inubashiri has
a reckless streak...

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.470
but he's a top fighter
and hardcore terrorist...

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:27.970
who's managed to
elude us many times.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.550
He's also a top-level Labor pilot.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:33.020
However, I'm not sure this is for us.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:37.600
I don't want your Labor team,
but look at this.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:41.820
What is it?

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.530
Built at Kronstadt Tank Works,

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:47.320
designed at the
Leningrad Science Academy...

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.320
it's the backbone
of the Soviet Army.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:54.290
Attack Labor L99.
NATO's code name is the "Doshka."

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:57.750
A "Red Labor" that has been
shrouded in a veil of secrecy.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:03.670
But it's arriving in Sakata tonight.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.630
Wh-What?!

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:09.680
This summer, the Soviets and
a certain southeast Asian nation...

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:13.310
signed a defense and weapons
procurement contract.

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:17.480
The Red Labor will
cement the deal.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.310
Well, how can I say,
this is top secret.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.440
It deported Nahodka on a
Soviet registered freighter...

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:27.400
in order to deflect any suspicion
by transporting it via the Sea of Japan.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:29.200
They're stopping in Sakata?

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:31.450
Seems too much
to be a coincidence.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.870
So, what do you want us to do?

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:36.870
I'd like you to dispatch your team.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:37.960
Sorry. I can't.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:40.790
Why not?

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:44.670
We can respond to requests
from the prefectural police...

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:49.010
but it takes a lot of red tape for us
to operate outside our jurisdiction.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:50.550
I came to see you...

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:54.050
because I want to avoid
going through the formal channels.

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:56.850
I thought that Division 2
was the kind of group...

00:06:56.890 --> 00:07:00.230
that didn't have qualms
about acting independently...

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:01.480
in order to prevent crimes.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.610
We have a terrible
misunderstanding, then.

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:07.440
Besides, we're not capable
of fighting advanced military Labors.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:09.950
You need the self-defense force.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:13.870
If I could've done that,
I wouldn't have ended up here!

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:16.790
And you call yourself
a police force?

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.750
We have this motto about
keeping everyone happy.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.000
Sorry about that.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:34.600
Then, how about this?

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:37.470
If it's too difficult
sending out your team...

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:41.640
how about you loan me
a few of your off-duty members?

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:44.480
Would that be appropriate?

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:49.440
How is it appropriate?
What can they do without Labors?

00:07:57.450 --> 00:08:00.410
What if I lend you two officers?

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.750
Oh, so you do understand!

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:04.580
Yes, I think I'm beginning to.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:06.380
Wonderful, wonderful!

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.840
Of course, expenses will
come from your budget.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:13.840
Something's fishy.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:16.970
Think of who you're talking about.
Of course it's fishy.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:19.930
Too bad you don't
get along with Public Safety.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:22.350
The only thing
we can be sure of is...

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:26.730
it involves a Labor
and the Home of the Sea terrorists.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:28.320
Sakata...

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:30.980
So, who are you going to send?

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:34.860
Sakata's known for...

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:35.990
Yes?

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:38.120
Hatahata.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:49.840
Why is he sending us out
to buy hatahata?

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:54.220
I think he meant that
we should go and enjoy ourselves.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:56.180
After all, we're off duty.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:59.390
I've always wanted to see
the Sea of Japan.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:02.060
And the mechanics gave us
money to buy stuff!

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:04.060
We ought to get them
very nice souvenirs.

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:09.820
Look. Does this look
like a vacation to you?

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.670
Asuma, look over there!

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:44.680
Um...

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:45.730
What?

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:47.230
Where's everyone else?

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:51.440
My men got off at Niigata and
took separate routes to Sakata.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:53.150
They're already in position.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:57.320
This line of work
requires the utmost in secrecy.

00:09:58.450 --> 00:09:59.030
Right...

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:04.160
I can't help feeling
kind of conspicuous, though.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:07.080
You are.
That's intentional.

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:11.210
That's exactly
why I wanted you here!

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:14.710
Your uniforms, your appearance,
and your actions...

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:17.920
make it very
clear and obvious that...

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:20.510
the Labor team is here
on the job in Sakata.

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.800
You're telling them all that...

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:27.140
we're here to prevent
the theft of the Doshka.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.850
What do you mean, "them"?

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:32.610
The Home of the Sea isn't
the only group after the Doshka.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:35.030
The fact that the Home of the Sea
knows about this...

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:38.650
just shows that the information
was leaked and has spread all over.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:42.950
The world's intelligence agents
won't just stand by and watch.

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:45.830
They've already marked you out.
Look around.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:47.700
The Russian ship crew
inside the store.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.750
They're all KGB.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:53.630
That man, that man,
and that one.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.000
That's not all.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:59.550
The British man eating ramen
over at that table.

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:01.260
He's SAS.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:02.260
No way!

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:06.220
All those American tourists
who just arrived out front.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.730
They're all CIA agents.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:11.400
NATO sent that couple.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:14.440
That dog crossing the road
is a Mossad spy dog.

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:18.820
And see that old lady
selling hatahata to Officer Izumi?

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:22.780
Her last job was assassinating
the head of the Chinese police.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.530
You're kidding, aren't you?

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:32.080
Let's call it a day.
You must be tired.

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.170
We've arranged lodging for you.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:40.550
What?!

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:43.590
Only one room? But we're...

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.510
There must be some mistake!

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:51.770
Mr. Takahata in Tokyo
sent in your reservations.

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:54.770
One night, two days
with breakfast, two people.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:58.780
Yuma Shinohara
and Akira Izumino.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:02.030
Can't you give us
an extra room now?

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:06.660
I had one, but it was
just taken a moment ago.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:10.580
Come on.
One night won't be so bad.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:15.960
I don't think
we have any choice.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:18.710
N-No choice? But, Asuma!

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:26.720
Boxer

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:31.730
Seaview

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:48.120
This won't work at all.
Right!

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:41.710
I'm disappointed in you,
Asuma!

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:47.840
Mr. Shinohara!
Phone call from Tokyo.

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:51.430
So I was going
for a midnight snack!

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:53.890
That was no reason to hit me!

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:04.650
Hello? Shinohara here.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.530
How's it going?

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.240
Captain, it's pretty rough here.

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:11.740
They're dragging us all over
the place in our uniforms!

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.240
And Noa hit me!

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:15.910
Izumi did? How come?

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:18.580
Never mind. What's up?

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:23.340
That Takahata sure spins
a pretty good tale.

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:27.630
He said his specialty
was the Soviet Union.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:31.970
So, why is he so concerned
with the Home of the Sea group?

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:35.020
That was odd,
so we checked him out.

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:41.400
Better not get caught off guard,
pretending you're tourists and all.

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:46.570
Yeah... Yeah, but...

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.570
What?!
Three hours from now?!

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:51.870
Defection?!

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:53.990
Right. I understand.

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:57.040
Shinohara and Izumi,
standing by for duty.

00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:59.370
What? Hatahata?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:02.130
Yeah, yeah,
we'll be sure to get you some!

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:34.530
Infiltration confirmed. Over.

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:42.270
It's going excellently, Chief.

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:45.310
Now it will look like
the Labor was stolen by terrorists.

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:51.150
But actually, the elusive Labor is a
present from a defecting KGB general.

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:55.070
The terrorist action will bring
all sorts of police and media running.

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:58.910
So long as our general stays shut up
in that thick armor, he'll be safe.

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:02.330
No matter how able and cunning
those foreign agents may be...

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:05.290
they won't be able to
act with all the press around.

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:10.170
That will give us a chance to run off
with both the Labor and the general.

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:14.170
Thanks to the Home of the Sea
and Special Vehicles...

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.510
for the magnificent diversion...

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:19.140
they both provided
without even knowing it.

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:21.010
A perfect plan.

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:23.100
Very clever.

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:27.900
To the criminal
inside the Labor!

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:30.860
Abandon your machine
and surrender to the police!

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.190
This is the Metropolitan Police!

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:35.070
Special Vehicles, Second Section.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:47.580
It's bad form
to use people like that.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:49.040
Damn you!

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:53.550
Are you sure
he won't shoot, Asuma?

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:55.970
It's a military vehicle in transit.

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:58.130
I'm sure it's not loaded
with live ammunition.

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:05.680
You Japs betrayed me!

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:08.600
Don't! Stop, stop!

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.190
Don't fire!

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:13.900
Take cover
behind the carrier, Noa!

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:15.990
If you take a direct hit
from the Doshka...

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:19.860
there's no way even the 98's
FRP armor would hold up!

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:21.620
You lied to me!

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:23.990
This is no time for arguing!

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:29.420
Miss Izumi, hurry.
Get behind the carrier.

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:46.770
This won't work.

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:51.270
Of course not! A 98 is useless
against a military Labor!

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:54.820
You were supposed to stay
quietly on the sidelines!

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.820
But you had to come out
like this!

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:59.990
You ruined my plan!
You'll take full responsibility for this!

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.320
Shut up!

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:05.950
That attitude of yours, of using
your own people like this caused this!

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:10.580
This isn't the time to argue.
What should I do, Asuma?

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:19.420
You did it this time.
You bastard!

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:30.270
Now we separate the men
from the boys!

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:57.050
Damn! I'm out of ammo!

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:00.340
Now, Noa!
Use the electromagnetic baton!

00:20:01.050 --> 00:20:02.970
Are you sure it will work?

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:04.140
Just do it!

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:16.650
Take this!

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:52.230
I'm freezing!

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:53.770
We did it!

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:58.400
Freeze! You're under arrest
for Labor theft!

00:20:58.650 --> 00:20:59.730
No fair!

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:03.740
This is why
everyone hates the police.

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:11.200
Ivan Ivanovitch Ivanovsky.

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:15.290
An apparently high-level KGB general
working on Labor development.

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:20.250
That junk about terrorism was
nothing but a big con job.

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:25.170
It was all a plan to divert
attention from the defection.

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:28.010
- That's about it.
- They fooled us, too.

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:29.550
It didn't make sense.

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:32.060
I don't know about
some elusive military Labor,

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:34.770
but we got our defector.

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:37.810
But the Yamagata Police
is upset as hell...

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:40.570
and the security division
issued a strong complaint.

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:43.480
But Public Safety came out
smelling like a rose.

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:46.110
So, everything's
being covered up again?

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:51.080
Well, I never liked the idea of any
of them having a weapon like that.

00:21:51.530 --> 00:21:53.370
And, in the end,
we are all on the same side.

00:21:53.490 --> 00:21:54.700
So why stir things up?

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:57.170
What about Takahata?

00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:59.540
He's being demoted.

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:02.630
That's his reward
for lying and using people.

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:04.670
A strategist done in
by his own plans.

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:07.590
You should watch out
for that, too, Goto.

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:13.470
Good work on a tough mission.
Take a break.

00:22:15.890 --> 00:22:18.730
By the way, where's my present?
Where's my hatahata?

00:22:21.310 --> 00:22:22.980
It's my favorite food!

00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:26.150
Don't tell me
you forgot my hatahata!

00:22:26.650 --> 00:22:28.780
I'm sorry, Sir, but...

00:22:29.360 --> 00:22:30.740
My hatahata!

00:22:42.590 --> 00:22:45.800
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:49.510
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.840 --> 00:22:55.770
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:05.270
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.400 --> 00:23:08.190
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:12.780
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:17.450
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:20.290
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:24.460
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:30.970
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.590 --> 00:23:36.220
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:36.180 --> 00:23:38.770
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.770 --> 00:23:41.980
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.230 --> 00:23:46.070
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.440 --> 00:23:52.240
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.410 --> 00:23:58.290
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:04.920
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:10.170
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:10.170
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:14.010 --> 00:24:17.310
Kanuka's grandmother, who was
visiting from Hawaii, had disappeared.

00:24:17.560 --> 00:24:21.060
Our only clue is a message about
Christmas 50 years ago?

00:24:21.270 --> 00:24:24.400
Captain,
can't we go out and find her?

00:24:24.560 --> 00:24:29.150
Well, there seems to be some
strange goings on at Teleport City.

00:24:29.150 --> 00:24:30.650
Could be difficult.

00:24:30.740 --> 00:24:33.070
Oh, come on.
What should we do?

00:24:33.450 --> 00:24:37.120
Next time. Eve's Trap.
Target, locked on!

00:24:35.450 --> 00:24:41.410
Next episode

